From: Beniamino Galvani <bgalvani@redhat.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 18:10:13 +0200
Subject: bpf: clat: fix sparc64 architecture define for BPF compilation

The cpu_arch_defines dictionary has no entry for sparc64, so the
fallback generates -D__sparc64__. However, sparc64 should be
identified by __sparc__ combined with __arch64__.

Fixes: fa9c00b595cc ('Add CLAT BPF program and build machinery')
---
 src/core/bpf/meson.build | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/core/bpf/meson.build b/src/core/bpf/meson.build
index fb75987..4bf817b 100644
--- a/src/core/bpf/meson.build
+++ b/src/core/bpf/meson.build
@@ -149,6 +149,7 @@ cpu_arch_defines = {
   'riscv64'     : ['-D__riscv', '-D__riscv_xlen=64', '-D__TARGET_ARCH_riscv'],
   'x86'         : ['-D__i386__', '-D__TARGET_ARCH_x86'],
   's390x'       : ['-D__s390__', '-D__s390x__', '-D__TARGET_ARCH_s390'],
+  'sparc64'     : ['-D__sparc__', '-D__arch64__', '-D__TARGET_ARCH_sparc'],
 
   # For arm, assume hardware fp is available.
   'arm'         : ['-D__arm__', '-D__ARM_PCS_VFP', '-D__TARGET_ARCH_arm'],
